# Hronaut Subscription and Trial License

Copyright 2026 Hronaut. All rights reserved except as expressly granted below.

## 1. Scope and acceptance

This license applies to Hronaut releases distributed with these terms, including source code and binaries. By installing, running, or modifying these releases, you agree to these terms. Earlier releases remain governed by the license supplied with them; this license does not revoke previously granted rights. Third-party components remain under their own licenses, as described in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

The source may be inspected. Source visibility does not grant unrestricted use, redistribution, sublicensing, or the right to provide Hronaut as a hosted service.

## 2. Ten-day evaluation

Each named user may evaluate Hronaut for personal or business purposes for one period of 10 consecutive days, starting with their first agent tool call. No payment card is required for this local trial, and it does not automatically convert into a paid subscription. Reinstallation, additional profiles, devices, or modified builds do not grant another evaluation period. You may not bypass or reset licensing controls.

## 3. Paid subscription

After the trial, all ongoing use requires an active paid subscription, including personal, educational, nonprofit, and commercial use. Each named-user seat permits that person to install, run, and internally modify Hronaut on up to three active devices. Seats cannot be shared concurrently and may be reassigned when the former user permanently stops using them. Internal modifications remain subject to these terms.

The price is USD $4 per named user per month or USD $24 per named user per year. The annual plan saves 50% compared with twelve monthly payments totaling $48, and is equivalent to $2/month billed annually. Applicable taxes and the final total are shown at checkout. Creem acts as Merchant of Record and handles payment, tax, invoices, renewals, and the billing portal.

## 4. Activation and validation

Creem supplies a license key after successful payment. Activate it in Hronaut Settings. The key is protected using operating-system secure storage. Hronaut periodically validates the subscription. A previously validated activation can remain usable offline for up to seven days after its last successful validation, subject to any earlier recorded subscription expiry. A confirmed invalid or revoked activation loses access when that result is processed.

## 5. Expiry and cancellation

Subscriptions renew automatically until canceled through https://www.creem.io/my-orders/login or support@hronaut.dev. Cancellation stops future renewal. Choose cancellation at the end of the paid period to retain access through that date; support uses this option unless you request immediate cancellation. Immediate cancellation ends the paid grant immediately. When a full subscription refund is processed, future renewals stop and the paid grant for the refunded period ends. Refunding an older payment does not end access paid for by a later, unrefunded payment. A partial goodwill refund does not by itself cancel the subscription, reduce seats, or end the paid grant. For a refund covering selected seats, the amount, affected seats, access end date, and future billing are agreed before processing; other seats retain access. Refund eligibility and exceptions are governed by the website Refund Policy, subject to mandatory law.

After trial or subscription expiry, agent automation is blocked. You retain limited permission to access existing local browser data manually for recovery, export, and deletion, and to manage licensing. Expiry does not delete your data. This recovery permission is not a free ongoing-use tier.

## 6. Restrictions and termination

You may not redistribute, resell, sublicense, publish copies of, or provide Hronaut itself as a hosted or managed service to third parties without separate written permission. You may not remove licensing controls or required notices. OEM distribution and embedded resale require separate written terms. These restrictions do not limit rights granted independently by third-party licenses or mandatory law.

Hronaut may suspend or terminate this grant for material breach, fraud, unlawful use, or payment failure. Where practical, notice and an opportunity to cure will be provided.

## 7. Updates, support, refunds, and liability

An active subscription includes generally available updates during the paid period, but not custom development or a guaranteed service level. Website Terms of Service and Refund Policy apply to purchases. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Hronaut is provided as is without warranties, and Hronaut is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages. Mandatory consumer rights are unaffected.

Licensing, billing, activation, cancellation, and refund questions: support@hronaut.dev.
